<description>Add I18nProvider mock to handle i18n dependencies</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import ImportedComponent from '../../modules/insights/insights-routing-view';

import { DataTableProvider } from "@calcom/features/data-table";
import { InsightsOrgTeamsProvider } from "@calcom/features/insights/context/InsightsOrgTeamsProvider";

// Mock I18nProvider to handle i18n dependencies
const I18nProvider = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => {
  return <>{children}</>;
};

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  // Since this component doesn't have any props, we don't need to use useParentState
  // However, we'll keep it here in case we need to add props in the future
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({});

  return (
    <I18nProvider>
      <DataTableProvider>
        <InsightsOrgTeamsProvider>
          <ImportedComponent />
        </InsightsOrgTeamsProvider>
      </DataTableProvider>
    </I18nProvider>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes:
1. Added a mock `I18nProvider` component that simply renders its children
2. Wrapped the entire component tree with the `I18nProvider`

This should help resolve the i18n-related dependency issues while allowing the preview to function properly. The mock provider will pass through any children components while satisfying the provider requirement in the component tree.

If you're still seeing errors, please let me know and I can help adjust the solution further. We might need to add more specific mocking for i18n functionality if the components require it.

